<title>SWITZERLAND: UBS lowers cash bond rates.</title>
<headline>UBS lowers cash bond rates.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Union Bank of Switzerland (UBS) said it was lowering the interest rate it pays on some of its cash bonds (Kassenobligationen) with effect from Thursday, February 13. It gave the following details:</p>
<p> Cash bonds	    New Rate	   Previous</p>
<p> Two-year		2.0 pct	    unchanged</p>
<p> Three-year	    2.25 pct	   2.5 pct</p>
<p> Four-year	     2.5 pct	    2.75 pct</p>
<p> Five-year	     2.75 pct	   3.0 pct</p>
<p> Six-year		3.0 pct	    3.25 pct</p>
<p> Seven-year	    3.25 pct	   3.50 pct</p>
<p> Eight-year	    3.5 pct	    3.75 pct</p>
<p>Note - Cash bonds, fixed-rate deposits for small investors, are used by banks to help finance their mortgage lending.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
